<article class="env-lemma" id="09KY">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/09KY">Lemma <span data-tag="09KY">22.22.3</span>.</a> Let $(A, \text{d})$ be a differential graded algebra. Let $M$ and $N$ be differential graded $A$-modules. </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
Let $P \to M$ be a P-resolution as in Lemma <a href="/tag/09KP" data-tag="09KP">22.20.4</a>. Then 
</p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits _{D(A, \text{d})}(M, N) = \mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits _{K(\text{Mod}_{(A, \text{d})})}(P, N)  \]
</div>
</li><li><p>
Let $N \to I$ be an I-resolution as in Lemma <a href="/tag/09KU" data-tag="09KU">22.21.4</a>. Then 
</p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits _{D(A, \text{d})}(M, N) = \mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits _{K(\text{Mod}_{(A, \text{d})})}(M, I)  \]
</div>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $P \to M$ be as in (1). Since $P \to M$ is a quasi-isomorphism we see that 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  \mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits _{D(A, \text{d})}(P, N) = \mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits _{D(A, \text{d})}(M, N)  \]
</div>
    <p>
       by definition of the derived category. A morphism $f : P \to N$ in $D(A, \text{d})$ is equal to $s^{-1}f'$ where $f' : P \to N'$ is a morphism and $s : N \to N'$ is a quasi-isomorphism. Choose a distinguished triangle 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  N \to N' \to Q \to N[1]  \]
</div>
    <p>
       As $s$ is a quasi-isomorphism, we see that $Q$ is acyclic. Thus $\mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits _{K(\text{Mod}_{(A, \text{d})})}(P, Q[k]) = 0$ for all $k$ by Lemma <a href="/tag/09KM" data-tag="09KM">22.20.2</a>. Since $\mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}\nolimits _{K(\text{Mod}_{(A, \text{d})})}(P, -)$ is cohomological, we conclude that we can lift $f' : P \to N'$ uniquely to a morphism $f : P \to N$. This finishes the proof. 
    <p>
      The proof of (2) is dual to that of (1) using Lemma <a href="/tag/09KS" data-tag="09KS">22.21.2</a> in stead of Lemma <a href="/tag/09KM" data-tag="09KM">22.20.2</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>